{
  "name": "Redstone language",
  "icon": "minecraft:comparator",
  "order": 10,
  "spoiler": false,
  "items": [],
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Held and struck",
      "text": [
        "Tribal machines hear redstone in two ways.",
        "A **held** signal pauses. Keep a line high and workshops, conductors, resonators, collectors, relays, braziers, meshes, fonts, pedestals, gate keystones and every generator except the Drumheart stop and wait. Storage and travel destinations lock.",
        "Nothing is ever lost to a pause: stored Pulse, items and fluids stay where they are.",
        "A **struck** signal, the rising edge when a line turns on, is a call. Only devices that do one discrete thing listen for it: a Drumheart takes a beat, a Ritual Brazier fires its seated rite, a Gate Keystone lights or darkens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading the camp",
      "text": [
        "Put a comparator against a Tribal block, facing away from it, to read what it holds without opening it: stored Pulse, how full its inventory or tank is, its FE buffer, or relay activity.",
        "For Pulse as a clean 0 to 15, use a [Pulse Gauge](pulse_gauge). When a number is not enough, crouch and right-click the block with this book for a sentence (see [Codex diagnostics](codex_diagnostics)).",
        "Clocks, levers and comparators are all you need to choreograph a whole camp."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Tribal wiring",
      "text": [
        "[Song Thread](song_thread) carries 0 to 15 weakly, like dust, in all six directions. It will not power the stone it touches, so it never latches.",
        "[Song plates](song_plates) output from their facing. Unary plates read their back; binary plates read left and right.",
        "[Verse Call and Answer](verse_link) carry a signal up to 32 blocks with no wire at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "A rite on a clock",
      "text": [
        "A Rite Pedestal holds and shows one item, and a comparator reads whether it is occupied. That is all a rite needs to run itself:",
        "- A relay restocks a pedestal of the [Rite Circle](rite_circle) with a tablet.",
        "- A Heartbeat plate, or a lever, strikes the brazier.",
        "- The rite fires and spends the tablet that matches the seated seal.",
        "- The comparator reports the pedestal empty, and the relay fills it again.",
        "Add a Memory plate if you want to arm and disarm the loop. The camp uses only the actions you could do by hand: no hidden extra inventory."
      ]
    },
